# Test pyramid

Same split as `05-nest-clean`:

| Layer | Test | Do not test |
|-------|------|-------------|
| **Unit (use case)** | Business rules, `Either` branches (`NotAllowedError`, `ResourceNotFoundError`), orchestration | HTTP status, JWT, Zod, Prisma wiring |
| **E2E (controller)** | Happy path: route, auth, validation, persistence end-to-end | Rules already covered in unit specs |

**Examples**

- `authorId !== recipe.authorId` → unit only (`edit-recipe.spec.ts`)
- Ingredient/tag dedup (`Ovo` vs `ovo`) → unit only (`create-recipe.spec.ts`)
- `PUT /recipes/:id` returns 204 and persists → e2e only (`edit-recipe.controller.e2e-spec.ts`)
- `POST /recipes` returns 201 and row exists → e2e happy path only (no dedup branch)

Do **not** duplicate use-case branches in e2e — including success paths for rules already covered in unit specs.

**E2e negative cases are justified only when**

- Auth guard rejects unauthenticated requests before the use case
- Controller maps specific errors to specific HTTP statuses (after MF-06)
- Middleware or pipe enforces policy outside the use case
